                                "sense_id": "364d2a91-c4e8-3252-b2a0-a7dd4d78040b",
                                "text": "„Die Annahme, die Homelands seien zu klein, beruhe auf der falschen Vorstellung, alle Afrikaner müssten in der Landwirtschaft tätig sein. Er behauptete über Pondoland, ‚that if a European nation which is accustomed to making great use of small and difficult land had lived there - if the Italians or the Danes, the Dutch or the English had lived here - those areas alone could perhaps have carried 19,000,000.‘“"
